   "title": "How to use · v1.0.0",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## How to use · v1.0.0\n\n**What it does:** SDXL base 1.0 text to image: one checkpoint file, 25 steps, 1024x1024 by default. Core ComfyUI nodes only.\n\n1. **Your inputs** (green group):\n   - **Prompt**: describe the picture in plain words or keywords.\n   - **Negative prompt**: what to avoid.\n   - **Size**: pick the shape; megapixels 1 = 1024x1024. SDXL was trained at about 1 megapixel, so leave megapixels at 1 and change only the shape (16:9 = 1344x768, 3:2 = 1280x832, 2:3 = 832x1280).\n   - **Steps** (25) and **CFG** (7): the template's values.\n   - **Seed**: a new one every run. Set \"control after generate\" to fixed to keep a picture.\n2. **Model**: the loader must show `sd_xl_base_1.0.safetensors` from the Downloads note. Nothing to change. Other SDXL checkpoints load here too (not tested).\n3. **Prompt**: nothing to change; the text comes from group 1.\n4. **Sampling**: dpmpp_2m / karras, from the official template. More pictures per run: `batch_size` on the **Empty picture** node here.\n5. Press **Run**. The picture is saved by the **Result** node to `output/SDXL/`.\n\n**What to expect:** on an RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell 24 GB, a 1024x1024 picture took 9 to 10 s (11 s on the first run, with the model load). Whole-GPU peak VRAM 7.6 to 10.0 GiB.\n\n**From the test runs**\n- Stay at megapixels 1. At megapixels 2 (1472x1472) the one test picture had two foxes instead of one, took 20 s and peaked at 12.9 GiB.\n- `batch_size` 2 took 19 s for the two pictures and peaked at 12.5 GiB on the 24 GB card.\n- Small errors are normal for the base model: in the default picture the fox's tail lies apart from its body. Change the seed.\n\n**Not in this workflow:** the SDXL refiner. The template does not use it and the model page says the base model can be used on its own.\n\n**Tested on:** RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell 24 GB, ComfyUI 0.45.3, 11 runs through the API on 2026-11-22. Not verified on a 12 GB card.\n"
   ]
  },
